Given the following text and a relational triplet extracted from it:

Text: Get emergency medical help if you have signs of an allergic reaction to levothyroxine: hives, difficult breathing, swelling of your face, lips, tongue, or throat. Allergic reactions are usually caused by the inactive ingredients in a product rather than by levothyroxine itself, so your doctor may suggest trying a different brand or form.
Levothyroxine may cause serious side effects. Call your doctor at once if you have:
- sudden pain or trouble moving your hip, wrist, or back;
- fast or irregular heartbeats, or a pounding heartbeat;
- chest pain, pain spreading to your jaw or shoulder;
- wheezing or shortness of breath;
- swelling in your legs or ankles, or new or worsening breathlessness when lying down;
- fever, swollen glands, itching, joint pain, or not feeling well;
- nausea, vomiting, or diarrhea;
- confusion or feeling disoriented;
- a seizure; or
- high blood sugar - increased thirst, increased urination, dry mouth, fruity breath odor.
Common levothyroxine side effects may include:
- fever, hot flashes, increased sweating, feeling too hot;
- tiredness;
Triplet: ["Levothyroxine", "has recommendation", "try different brand or form"]

The relation 'has recommendation' in the triplet is defined as 'A healthcare provider may suggest altering the product form or brand in response to the specified condition or issue.' In this context, is there any relation appropriate to replace it? Choose a relation whose meaning and subject/object direction match the triplet even if the wording differs; choose 'None of the above' only if no candidate fits. Please answer by providing only the letter of your choice.

Choices:
A. 'may require dose adjustment': The subject medication might need a change in dosage under certain conditions or over time.
B. 'requires patient to read': The patient is required to review the specified educational materials or documentation related to the medication.
C. 'should inform doctor about': Patients taking the subject drug should tell their doctor about the condition or circumstance specified by the object entity.
D. 'has brand name': The subject drug is marketed under the brand or trade name specified by the object entity.
E. 'requires monitoring of': Patients taking the subject drug may need the medical test or monitoring specified by the object entity.
F. None of the above.

Answer:
